# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository.
#
# Without this, an editor writing CRLF turns any later edit into a whole-file
# rewrite: the real change hides inside hundreds of phantom deleted lines and
# the file conflicts with everything else touching it.
#
# eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf, so working copies get LF on every platform,
# not just what git stores. That is deliberate: every editor in use here reads
# LF fine, and leaving checkout to a per-developer setting is what produced the
# mixed endings in the first place.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary and generated content git must not touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.dll binary
uv.lock -diff linguist-generated
